│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduced_ising_ansatz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 146 parameters with very high accuracy (100% on all sets), but    │
│                          │ the parameter efficiency score is only 0.01, indicating we're using too many parameters.  │
│                          │ The goal is to dramatically reduce the parameter count while maintaining accuracy on this │
│                          │ small training set.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. We have 100% accuracy on train/val/test, suggesting we can afford to remove parameters │
│                          │ 2. With 8 qubits and only a few training examples, we're likely overfitting               │
│                          │ 3. Parameter efficiency dominates the combined score, so reducing parameters is critical  │
│                          │ 4. Current architecture has 8 RY params + 16 RZ params = 24 per-qubit parametrized gates  │
│                          │ + linear chain entanglement                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Replace the redundant per-qubit RY and RZ layers with shared/reduced parametrization    │
│                          │ - Use parametrized two-qubit gates (CRZ, XX, YY, ZZ) to create entanglement with fewer    │
│                          │ unique parameters through parameter sharing                                               │
│                          │ - Reduce total gate count while maintaining expressivity                                  │
│                          │ - Consolidate RZ layers into the parametrized two-qubit interactions                      │
│                          │ - Use a single parameter (or few parameters) shared across similar positions to reduce    │
│                          │ complexity                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new design:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Use a single shared RY parameter repeated across all qubits for initial rotation (or a  │
│                          │ few shared parameters)                                                                    │
│                          │ - Replace fixed CZ chain with parametrized two-qubit gates (CRZ or XX/YY) using shared    │
│                          │ parameters                                                                                │
│                          │ - Eliminate or drastically reduce the redundant post-CZ RZ layer                          │
│                          │ - This maintains entanglement pattern but with ~10-15 parameters instead of 24            │
