│ patch_description        │ The current model achieves perfect accuracy but suffers from extremely poor parameter     │
│                          │ efficiency (0.01). With 146 parameters and perfect test accuracy, the model is            │
│                          │ over-parameterized. The key bottleneck for the combined score is parameter economy.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Aggressive parameter sharing: Use only 4 unique parameters instead of 40 by sharing RY │
│                          │ and RZ parameters across qubits                                                           │
│                          │ 2. This reduces the parameter count by 90% while maintaining expressivity through:        │
│                          │    - Shared RY rotation (rotates all qubits in the same way initially)                    │
│                          │    - Shared RZ pre-entanglement (uniform phase)                                           │
│                          │    - CZ linear chain (provides qubit-specific entanglement)                               │
│                          │    - Shared RZ post-entanglement (uniform phase after entanglement)                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should dramatically improve parameter efficiency while maintaining accuracy, since   │
│                          │ the current model is already perfectly accurate on all sets.                              │
