│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ultra_minimal_rz_unified                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the prior programs shows:                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Program 1 (score 0.68): 20 parameters (separate rz_pre and rz_post), converges in 60   │
│                          │ steps                                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. Program 2 (score 0.72): 14 parameters (unified rz_shared), but converges in 90 steps   │
│                          │ 3. Current program (score 0.68): 20 parameters, same as Program 1                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that Program 2 achieves the best score (0.72) with the fewest          │
│                          │ parameters (14), despite slightly slower convergence. The unified RZ layer after          │
│                          │ entanglement is highly efficient.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ However, Program 2 uses two distinct parameters ("ry_shared" and "rz_shared"), with       │
│                          │ rz_shared appearing both before and after the CZ entanglement layer. To further improve   │
│                          │ parameter efficiency while maintaining accuracy, I will:                                  │
│                          │ - Keep the unified RZ parameter that appears both pre- and post-entanglement (this is     │
│                          │ what makes Program 2 effective)                                                           │
│                          │ - Maintain separate RY parameter for expressivity on the rotation axis                    │
│                          │ - This keeps us at 2 unique parameters total, matching Program 2's minimal footprint      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The ultra-minimal approach ensures maximum parameter efficiency (matching the best prior  │
│                          │ result) while maintaining perfect accuracy and good convergence. This aligns with the     │
│                          │ scoring metric that heavily weights parameter economy.                                    │
