                         Patch Metadata - Gen 18/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ param_share_and_parametric_entangler                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses 38 parameters (alternating "a" and "b" suffixes), which results  │
│                          │ in poor parameter efficiency (0.03) and lower combined score (0.64).                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of prior programs shows:                                                         │
│                          │ - Prior program 2 (14 params, score 0.72): Used maximum parameter sharing with one shared │
│                          │ RY and one shared RZ parameter, achieving the best score.                                 │
│                          │ - Prior program 1 (20 params, score 0.68): Used separate pre/post RZ parameters.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program regresses by using too many parameters without improving performance. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Proposed improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ 1. **Maximize parameter sharing**: Return to highly shared parameters (3 total:           │
│                          │ ry_shared, rz_pre_shared, rz_post_shared) to restore parameter efficiency.                │
│                          │ 2. **Parametrize entanglement**: Replace each fixed CZ gate with CRZ using a single       │
│                          │ shared "phi_ent" parameter. This gives the optimizer direct control over entanglement     │
│                          │ strength while adding only one parameter, improving controllability without significant   │
│                          │ parameter cost.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
