│ patch_name               │ rx_single_rz_cz                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current parametrized two-qubit CRZ gates with fixed CZ gates, and swap the RY │
│                          │ rotation to RX. This combines:                                                            │
│                          │ 1. The parameter-efficient single-RZ design from prior program 2 (which scored 0.72, best │
│                          │ score)                                                                                    │
│                          │ 2. The axis-swap hypothesis from the recommendation (RX instead of RY)                    │
│                          │ 3. The fixed CZ chain (reliable in prior programs)                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program wastes parameters with 26 parameters and CRZ gates but scores only    │
│                          │ 0.66. Prior program 2 achieved 0.72 with just 14 parameters using CZ instead. This edit   │
│                          │ reduces to 2 parameters while exploring whether RX/RZ/CZ combo matches or exceeds         │
│                          │ RY/RZ/CZ performance on this task.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome: Match or exceed prior program 2's score (0.72) with minimal parameters  │
│                          │ and faster convergence.                                                                   │
