│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests swapping the shared RY layer for RX to test if a different    │
│                          │ rotation axis yields better expressivity or parameter efficiency.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Analysis of prior results:**                                                            │
│                          │ - Program 1 (20 params, score 0.68): RY + RZ_pre + CZ + RZ_post                           │
│                          │ - Program 2 (14 params, score 0.72): RY + RZ + CZ + RZ (unified RZ layer)                 │
│                          │ - Current (26 params, score 0.66): RY + RZ_pre + XX chain + RZ_post                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program has regressed (score 0.66) despite perfect accuracy across            │
│                          │ train/val/test. The issue is likely **parameter bloat** (26 params vs 14 in best) and the │
│                          │ XX Ising gates adding overhead without sufficient benefit. Convergence is faster (30      │
│                          │ steps) but parameter efficiency (0.04) is worse than Program 2 (0.07).                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed fix:**                                                                         │
│                          │ Replace RY with RX in the first layer, keeping the RZ sandwich and CZ chain structure     │
│                          │ from Program 1 (which scored 0.68). This:                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Tests if RX provides better expressivity for this problem                              │
│                          │ 2. Returns to a proven 3-parameter structure (rx_shared, rz_pre_shared, rz_post_shared)   │
│                          │ 3. Reduces parameters from 26 to 3, dramatically improving parameter efficiency           │
│                          │ 4. Maintains the CZ entanglement which was effective in prior programs                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The RX/RZ combination may offer orthogonal expressivity compared to RY/RZ, potentially    │
│                          │ improving generalization while maintaining high accuracy with far fewer parameters.       │
