│ patch_name               │ hybrid_cz_xx_minimal                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best features of the prior programs:                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the best performer (score 0.72, n_params=14)**: The CZ entanglement pattern     │
│                          │ with unified RZ parameter sharing provides excellent parameter efficiency with only 14    │
│                          │ parameters. This achieves perfect accuracy with minimal parameter overhead.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the current program (score 0.66, n_params=26)**: The XX parametrized gates      │
│                          │ replace CZ fixed gates, providing additional expressivity through parameterized two-qubit │
│                          │ interactions.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Crossover strategy**: Replace the CZ gates with XX gates while keeping the single RZ │
│                          │ parameter unified (not split into pre/post). This combines:                               │
│                          │    - The parameter efficiency of unified RZ sharing (14 params → 1 RZ param)              │
│                          │    - The potential expressivity gain from parametrized XX gates (7 params)                │
│                          │    - Total: 8 (RY) + 1 (RZ) + 7 (XX) = 16 parameters                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the best score (0.72) uses unified RZ sharing with CZ gates. By   │
│                          │ replacing CZ with parametrized XX gates while maintaining the efficient parameter         │
│                          │ structure, we preserve the excellent accuracy while potentially improving convergence and │
│                          │ generalization through better expressivity of the parametrized interaction layer.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This avoids the parameter explosion (26 params) of the current program while adding back  │
│                          │ the expressivity of parametrized interactions.                                            │
