│                          │ the first prior                                                                           │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency is critical: 14 params >> 20 params in the scoring function        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Crossover strategy:**                                                                   │
│                          │ Take the single-block CZ architecture from the second prior (best efficiency at score     │
│                          │ 0.72) as the foundation. This maintains:                                                  │
│                          │ - 14 trainable parameters (optimal parameter count)                                       │
│                          │ - Depth 35 (optimal circuit depth)                                                        │
│                          │ - Superior accuracy matching with minimal parameters                                      │
│                          │ - Fast convergence (60-90 steps)                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The single-block structure provides better parameter efficiency without sacrificing       │
│                          │ accuracy compared to the two-block version while being significantly simpler than the     │
│                          │ current XX-based approach.                                                                │
