╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rz_pre_post                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Split the shared Z-rotation parameter into independent pre- and post-entanglement phases. │
│                          │ The current architecture reuses the same `rz_shared` parameter for all RZ gates (before   │
│                          │ and after the CZ chain). By introducing separate parameters `rz_pre` (before CZ) and      │
│                          │ `rz_post` (after CZ), the optimizer gains independent control over phase rotations at     │
│                          │ different stages of the ansatz.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This increases n_params from 2 to 3 (ry_shared, rz_pre, rz_post) but enables the          │
│                          │ optimizer to:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Learn distinct optimal rotations for pre- and post-entanglement phases                 │
│                          │ 2. Better capture the different roles these phases play in the quantum state evolution    │
│                          │ 3. Potentially improve convergence speed (currently 150 steps) while maintaining accuracy │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a proven sandwich template strategy where layer-wise tuning of phase rotations    │
│                          │ improves trainability.                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0141                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
