│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rz_pre_post                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Split the shared RZ rotations into separate pre-entanglement (rz_pre) and                 │
│                          │ post-entanglement (rz_post) parameters. Currently, both RZ layers before and after the CZ │
│                          │ chain share the same parameter value, which constrains the optimizer. By allowing         │
│                          │ independent RZ rotations before and after entanglement, the optimizer gains more          │
│                          │ expressive power to learn layer-specific phase transformations. This sandwich structure   │
│                          │ (RY → RZ_pre → CZ → RZ_post) is a well-known quantum ansatz pattern that benefits from    │
│                          │ independent pre- and post-entanglement phase control. The parameter count increases       │
│                          │ modestly from 14 to 16 (only +2 parameters per block), which should have minimal impact   │
│                          │ on parameter efficiency while potentially improving convergence speed and generalization. │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
