                         Patch Metadata - Gen 35/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crz_shared_entangling                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace all CZ gates in the entangling ladder with shared-parameter CRZ gates. The CZ     │
│                          │ gate is a special case of CRZ(π), but by making it parametrized with a shared parameter   │
│                          │ across all positions, the optimizer gains direct control over the entangling angle. This  │
│                          │ approach:                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Maintains parameter economy: adds only 1 parameter (shared across 7 CRZ gates) instead │
│                          │ of 7 independent XX parameters                                                            │
│                          │ 2. Keeps total parameters at ~15 (vs 20 in current, matching prior successful models)     │
│                          │ 3. Improves optimizer flexibility: CRZ gates can be learned to arbitrary angles,          │
│                          │ potentially converging faster than fixed CZ                                               │
│                          │ 4. Preserves the proven linear entangling topology that achieved perfect accuracy in      │
│                          │ prior programs                                                                            │
│                          │ 5. Allows the optimizer to discover optimal entangling strength during training           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is more parameter-efficient than the current XX approach while maintaining the       │
│                          │ architectural properties that led to high performance.                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0165                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
