│                          │ 1. Removes the XX Ising layer (which added 8 gates and 1 parameter) and returns to the    │
│                          │ proven CZ chain                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Adds a prepended global RX layer across all qubits (using a shared "rx_shared"         │
│                          │ parameter) to explore initial X-rotation for enhanced state-space coverage                │
│                          │ 3. Keeps the core Y→Z sandwich + linear CZ backbone structure                             │
│                          │ 4. Results in only 3 parameters (rx_shared, ry_shared, rz_shared) instead of 20,          │
│                          │ dramatically improving parameter efficiency while maintaining accuracy                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines the best of both approaches: the minimal parameter count that achieved 0.72 │
│                          │ plus an additional cross-axis rotation to potentially improve convergence and             │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
