│ patch_name               │ split_rz_phases_single_block                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current double-block structure (which redundantly repeats the ansatz with the │
│                          │ same parameters, unnecessarily doubling depth to 65) with a single-block ansatz that      │
│                          │ splits the shared RZ parameter into independent pre- and post-entanglement phases. This   │
│                          │ maintains the proven accuracy while:                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Reducing depth from 65 back to 35 (eliminating the redundant second block)             │
│                          │ 2. Increasing learnable parameters from 14 to 15 (minimal overhead, still highly          │
│                          │ parameter-efficient)                                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Granting independent tuning of pre-entanglement and post-entanglement phase shifts,    │
│                          │ which can improve model expressiveness without increasing gate count                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly addresses parameter economy by removing redundancy while introducing        │
│                          │ meaningful expressiveness through phase differentiation.                                  │
