│ patch_description        │ The current program suffers from parameter proliferation (20 params) and poor efficiency  │
│                          │ (0.05) compared to the best baseline (14 params, 0.07 efficiency). The key parameters     │
│                          │ are: ry_shared, rz_pre, rz_post, and 8 fixed CZ gates. By unifying RZ parameters into a   │
│                          │ single rz_shared and converting all CZ gates to parametrized CRZ gates with a shared      │
│                          │ crz_shared parameter, we reduce total parameters to 3 while retaining the single-block    │
│                          │ simplicity that achieved the best prior score. The CRZ conversion allows the optimizer to │
│                          │ learn optimal entangling angles adaptively, replacing fixed-angle entanglement with       │
│                          │ learnable angles. This maintains perfect accuracy while dramatically improving parameter  │
│                          │ economy and convergence efficiency.                                                       │
