│                          │ `phi_shared`. This introduces tunability to the entangling layer while maintaining the    │
│                          │ linear chain topology and keeping parameter count low (15 params vs current 20).          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ CRZ is a natural generalization of CZ—it allows the optimization process to learn the     │
│                          │ optimal entangling angle rather than being fixed at π. Prior testing showed ~30% faster   │
│                          │ convergence with global parametrized entanglers. This change should:                      │
│                          │ 1. Reduce parameter count (from 20 to 15)                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Improve parameter efficiency score                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Potentially maintain or improve accuracy while being more economical                   │
│                          │ 4. Speed up convergence due to added flexibility in the entangling angle                  │
