│ patch_name               │ block_specific_params_with_cz_chain                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current single-block XX-chain design (score 0.68) has too many parameters (20) and    │
│                          │ poor parameter efficiency (0.05). Prior two-block designs with CZ chains achieved 0.72    │
│                          │ with 14 params by maintaining full parameter sharing.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation to introduce block-specific specialization, we will:         │
│                          │ 1. Return to the proven CZ-chain architecture (simpler, more efficient than XX)           │
│                          │ 2. Add a second identical block                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Use block-specific parameters: block 1 uses ry_1/rz_1, block 2 uses ry_2/rz_2          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This allows each deep sandwich (block) to learn different features while maintaining high │
│                          │ parameter economy. Expected: ~18 params, better parameter efficiency, improved            │
│                          │ expressivity beyond uniform design.                                                       │
