│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rx_prepend_single_block_optimized                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves perfect accuracy (1.00) but with only 14 parameters and a    │
│                          │ score of 0.72. Analysis of prior programs shows:                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter Economy**: The single-block version (14 params, depth 35) achieves the     │
│                          │ same accuracy as the double-block version (14 params, depth 65) but with half the depth   │
│                          │ and gate count, suggesting parameter sharing is very effective.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Key Insight**: Both prior programs use only 2 trainable parameters (ry_shared and    │
│                          │ rz_shared) despite appearing to have 14 "param slots" - this is due to aggressive         │
│                          │ parameter sharing across all 8 qubits and both blocks.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Proposed Optimization**:                                                             │
│                          │    - Add a prepended global RX layer with a new `rx_shared` parameter to diversify the    │
│                          │ initial state manifold                                                                    │
│                          │    - Keep only a SINGLE block (not two) to minimize depth while maintaining expressivity  │
│                          │    - This adds 1 new parameter (rx_shared) for a total of 3 parameters                    │
│                          │    - Should maintain or improve accuracy while reducing convergence steps and improving   │
│                          │ parameter efficiency                                                                      │
│                          │    - The RX+RY+RZ sandwich provides better coverage of the SU(2) manifold than RY+RZ      │
│                          │ alone                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Expected Benefits**:                                                                 │
│                          │    - Better parameter efficiency (3 params vs 14 reported)                                │
│                          │    - Reduced depth (from 65 to ~40)                                                       │
│                          │    - Faster convergence due to richer initial diversification                             │
│                          │    - Maintained accuracy on this well-learned task                                        │
