│ patch_name               │ ry_rz_cz_single_layer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the three programs shows they all achieve perfect accuracy (1.00) with        │
│                          │ identical parameter efficiency (0.07) and 14 parameters, but differ significantly in      │
│                          │ computational efficiency:                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Current program (RX-based)**: Uses RX instead of RY, has lowest depth (29) and gate  │
│                          │ count (138), but slowest convergence (120 steps)                                          │
│                          │ 2. **Prior program 1 (double-layer RY)**: Uses RY with two identical layers, higher depth │
│                          │ (65) and gates (372), but faster convergence (90 steps)                                   │
│                          │ 3. **Prior program 2 (single-layer RY)**: Uses single RY layer, medium depth (35) and     │
│                          │ gates (186), matching convergence (90 steps)                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that **RY outperforms RX for this task** (prior programs achieve       │
│                          │ better convergence), but the **single-layer approach is superior** to double-layer        │
│                          │ (maintains accuracy with half the depth/gates).                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Crossover strategy**: Combine the single-layer structure (Prior program 2) with RY      │
│                          │ gates, maintaining the efficient CZ chain and the final RZ layer. This should:            │
│                          │ - Keep the proven RY initialization (better than RX)                                      │
│                          │ - Eliminate redundant double-layer duplication                                            │
│                          │ - Maintain perfect accuracy with faster convergence than current RX version               │
│                          │ - Achieve better parameter economy by having a clean single-layer design                  │
