                         Patch Metadata - Gen 51/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_entangler_with_adaptive_rotations                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign improves upon the current program by:                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Hybrid entangling strategy**: Block 1 uses fixed CZ gates for stability, while Block │
│                          │ 2 uses parametrized CRZ gates with a shared parameter to enable faster convergence and    │
│                          │ better expressivity, similar to the successful recommendation.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Reduced parameter count**: By using only 3 trainable parameters (rx_shared,          │
│                          │ rz_shared, and crz_shared) across 2 blocks instead of 20, we maximize parameter economy   │
│                          │ while maintaining full connectivity.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Improved convergence**: The parametrized CRZ in block 2 allows the circuit to adapt  │
│                          │ the entanglement strength dynamically, which should reduce convergence steps              │
│                          │ significantly (from 60 towards ~30-40).                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Better generalization**: Fewer parameters reduce overfitting risk and should close   │
│                          │ any generalization gap while maintaining perfect accuracy on small training sets.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Gate depth optimization**: Removes redundant RZ pre/post decomposition in favor of   │
│                          │ unified rotation layers that serve dual purposes (state preparation and rotation between  │
│                          │ entanglement blocks).                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The architecture follows: [RX-all] → [RZ-all] → [CZ-chain] → [RZ-all] in block 1, then    │
│                          │ [RX-all] → [RZ-all] → [CRZ-chain] → [RZ-all] in block 2, allowing the hybrid approach to  │
│                          │ test if mixed entanglers improve convergence while keeping total parameters low.          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0162                                                                                   │
