│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rz_pre_post                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single shared RZ parameter with two independent RZ parameters: one applied    │
│                          │ before the CZ chain (rz_pre) and one after (rz_post). This allows independent control     │
│                          │ over phases inserted immediately before and after entanglement, enabling finer            │
│                          │ interference tuning without increasing parameter count or depth. The circuit structure    │
│                          │ remains [RX]→[RZ_pre]→[CZ-chain]→[RZ_post], but with two parameter degrees of freedom     │
│                          │ instead of one, which should improve convergence speed and potentially reduce the         │
│                          │ training gap by better utilizing the available phase landscape around the critical        │
│                          │ entanglement layer.                                                                       │
