│ patch_description        │ Revert to the proven RY→RZ→CZ→RZ motif from the prior high-scoring programs (0.72), which │
│                          │ achieved perfect accuracy with excellent parameter efficiency. The current program uses   │
│                          │ parametrized CRZ gates and 20 parameters, scoring only 0.68. Instead, implement the       │
│                          │ recommendation to split RZ control into "rz_pre" (before CZ chain) and "rz_post" (after   │
│                          │ CZ chain), providing independent phase control before and after entanglement for          │
│                          │ fine-tuning interference timing. This reduces parameters from 20 to just 3 (ry_shared,    │
│                          │ rz_pre, rz_post) while maintaining the high expressivity of the RY→RZ→CZ→RZ structure.    │
│                          │ The prior single-block variant with 14 params and depth 35 suggests one block is          │
│                          │ sufficient; using shared parameters across blocks maximizes economy while preserving      │
│                          │ accuracy.                                                                                 │
