│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rz_pre_post_split                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses XX parametrized two-qubit gates with a shared parameter, which   │
│                          │ increased the parameter count to 20 while maintaining accuracy. However, this added       │
│                          │ complexity without improving the combined score (0.68 vs 0.72 for the prior single-block  │
│                          │ design).                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight from the prior programs is that the RY→RZ→CZ→RZ motif with just 2         │
│                          │ parameters (ry_shared and rz_shared) achieved a combined score of 0.72 with minimal       │
│                          │ parameter overhead. The recommendation to split rz_shared into rz_pre (before             │
│                          │ entanglement) and rz_post (after entanglement) will provide finer control over phase      │
│                          │ evolution timing without increasing depth.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Replaces the XX chain (which requires an extra parameter) with the proven CZ chain     │
│                          │ 2. Splits the single rz_shared parameter into rz_pre and rz_post for phase control        │
│                          │ before/after entanglement                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Reduces parameters from 20 to 3 (ry_shared, rz_pre, rz_post), improving                │
│                          │ parameter_efficiency                                                                      │
│                          │ 4. Maintains the RY initialization for amplitude control                                  │
│                          │ 5. Uses a single-block architecture (proven to work well) rather than repeated blocks     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This configuration leverages the symmetry of the problem while allowing independent       │
│                          │ tuning of pre- and post-entanglement phases, which can capture more subtle interference   │
│                          │ patterns with fewer degrees of freedom.                                                   │
