│ patch_description        │ The current program uses 20 parameters with separate rz_pre and rz_post, yielding a score │
│                          │ of 0.68. The prior single-block version (14 params) achieved 0.72. The issue is           │
│                          │ over-parameterization without corresponding benefit.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit replaces the fixed CZ chain with a shared-parameter CRZ chain, following the    │
│                          │ recommendation that "CRZ chains converge ~30% faster." This approach:                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Keeps the simple single-block structure (proven effective at score 0.72)               │
│                          │ 2. Replaces 7 fixed CZ gates with 7 CRZ gates sharing one parameter "phi_ent"             │
│                          │ 3. Reduces total parameters from 20 to 16 (vs 14 in prior, but with enhanced              │
│                          │ expressivity)                                                                             │
│                          │ 4. Provides learnable entanglement strength while maintaining parameter economy           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The CRZ parametrization allows the optimizer to control entanglement dynamically,         │
│                          │ expected to improve convergence speed and generalization.                                 │
