│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ alternating_ising_crz_hybrid                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses 20 parameters with shared XX gates, achieving 0.68 score. Prior  │
│                          │ successful attempts achieved 0.72 with only 14 parameters using simpler CZ chains and     │
│                          │ RY/RZ rotations.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight from prior metrics is that:                                               │
│                          │ 1. Fewer parameters (14 vs 20) achieved better scores (0.72 vs 0.68)                      │
│                          │ 2. CZ chains were more parameter-efficient than XX chains                                 │
│                          │ 3. The problem achieves perfect accuracy with minimal parameters, suggesting it benefits  │
│                          │ from sparsity and controlled expressivity                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This new approach hybridizes entanglement strategies:                                     │
│                          │ - Block 1: Uses a CZ chain (fixed, non-parametrized) for stable, economical entanglement  │
│                          │ - Block 2: Uses CRZ gates with a single shared parameter for adaptive, parameterized      │
│                          │ entanglement                                                                              │
│                          │ - Single-qubit rotations: Alternates between RY and RZ with shared parameters for better  │
│                          │ expressivity with fewer params                                                            │
│                          │ - Reduced parameter footprint: Only 3 parameters (ry_shared, rz_shared, phi_crz) vs 20 in │
│                          │ current approach                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design:                                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Recovers the parameter efficiency of the best prior solution (14 params) by using CZ + │
│                          │ CRZ chains                                                                                │
│                          │ 2. Adds controlled expressivity through CRZ in the second block without parameter         │
│                          │ explosion                                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Uses alternating single-qubit rotations to maximize expressivity per parameter         │
│                          │ 4. Should converge faster (prior convergence was ~90 steps with 14 params) due to reduced │
│                          │ parameter count                                                                           │
