│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rz_phase_control                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Split the single shared RZ parameter into separate pre- and post-entanglement phases.     │
│                          │ Currently all RZ gates use "rz_shared", which means the same phase is applied before and  │
│                          │ after the CZ chain. By splitting into "rz_pre" (before CZ) and "rz_post" (after CZ), we   │
│                          │ enable finer interference control and potentially better generalization. This increases   │
│                          │ parameters from 2 to 3 (ry_shared, rz_pre, rz_post) while maintaining maximal parameter   │
│                          │ sharing across blocks. The extra parameter provides an additional degree of freedom for   │
│                          │ phase tuning without significantly increasing circuit depth or gate count, addressing the │
│                          │ recommendation for split phase control around the CZ sandwich.                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0288                                                                                   │
