│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_rz_phases_single_block                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program unnecessarily repeats the same 3-block structure 3 times with fully   │
│                          │ shared parameters (ry_shared, rz_shared). This creates excessive depth (95) and gate      │
│                          │ count (558) without improving accuracy or generalization.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insight: Program #2 (single block, 14 params) achieved identical perfect accuracy     │
│                          │ with 1/3 the depth. The repetition adds no value.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Proposed improvement:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Reduce to single block architecture (like Program #2)                                  │
│                          │ 2. Split the RZ gate into independent pre-entanglement (rz_pre) and post-entanglement     │
│                          │ (rz_post) phases                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. This gives 3 total parameters (ry_shared, rz_pre, rz_post) instead of 2                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Benefits:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Dramatically reduces depth from 95 to 35 (improves parameter economy scoring)           │
│                          │ - Reduces gate count from 558 to 186 (improves efficiency)                                │
│                          │ - Adds only 1 parameter while gaining phase control around the CZ chain                   │
│                          │ - Maintains perfect accuracy while enabling finer interference tuning                     │
│                          │ - Faster convergence (should mirror Program #2's ~90 steps)                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The split RZ phases allow the optimizer to independently control single-qubit rotations   │
│                          │ before and after entanglement, which is known to improve expressivity in parameterized    │
│                          │ circuits with minimal parameter overhead.                                                 │
