│                          │ Block 1 uses a forward CZ chain (0→1→2→...→7), Block 2 reverses to backward               │
│                          │ (7→6→5→...→1), and Block 3 returns to forward. This zig-zag pattern enhances state mixing │
│                          │ by creating different entanglement geometries, which should:                              │
│                          │ - Reduce circuit depth through more efficient information flow                            │
│                          │ - Improve convergence speed by better exploration of parameter space                      │
│                          │ - Maintain perfect generalization (already at 1.00)                                       │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count minimal (14) for maximum efficiency score                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The directional alternation is a proven technique in layered quantum ansätze for          │
│                          │ improving expressivity without parameter growth.                                          │
