│ patch_description        │ The current program uses separate parameter names (rz_pre, rz_post) instead of parameter  │
│                          │ sharing, which increased n_params from 14 to 20 and reduced the score from 0.72 to 0.68.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Restores parameter sharing by using only "ry_shared" and "rz_shared" throughout all    │
│                          │ blocks                                                                                    │
│                          │ 2. Appends a fourth identical RY→RZ→CZ-chain→RZ block                                     │
│                          │ 3. Maintains only 2 trainable parameters while increasing circuit depth and gate count    │
│                          │ 4. Follows the proven pattern that achieved 0.72 with parameter-efficient architectures   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior 3-block variant showed that repeating the same block structure with shared      │
│                          │ parameters maintains high accuracy (1.00 on all metrics) while improving convergence      │
│                          │ (from 90 to 30 steps) and parameter efficiency. Adding a fourth block should further      │
│                          │ improve these metrics while staying within parameter constraints.                         │
