│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_fourth_block_reverse_chains                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves perfect accuracy but converges slowly (90 steps). The prior  │
│                          │ 3-block program with alternating CZ-chain directions (forward → reverse → forward)        │
│                          │ achieved much faster convergence (30 steps) despite the same parameter count.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit adds a fourth block with reversed CZ-chain (7→6→...→0) following the third      │
│                          │ block's forward chain. This:                                                              │
│                          │ - Extends the alternating pattern shown to accelerate convergence                         │
│                          │ - Increases gate-to-parameter ratio from ~26 to ~35 gates/param (186 → 372 gates with     │
│                          │ same 14 params in seed to 558 gates in 3-block, we expect ~744 gates in 4-block)          │
│                          │ - Reuses only the two shared parameters (ry_shared, rz_shared), keeping parameter count   │
│                          │ minimal                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Maintains the RY→RZ→CZ-chain→RZ structure proven effective                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected benefit: Faster convergence (potentially matching the 30-step convergence of the │
│                          │ 3-block variant) while maintaining 100% accuracy and high parameter efficiency.           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0253                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
