│ patch_description        │ The current program repeats an identical RY→RZ→CZ-chain→RZ block four times with full     │
│                          │ parameter sharing, which creates a very deep circuit (depth 125, gate count 744) while    │
│                          │ maintaining only 14 parameters. This extreme depth causes inefficient optimization and    │
│                          │ slow convergence relative to the gate complexity.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The redesigned architecture alternates between RX and RY rotations across blocks while    │
│                          │ maintaining tight parameter sharing. This provides greater expressivity variation per     │
│                          │ parameter without adding new parameters, reduces circuit depth by breaking the rigid      │
│                          │ repetitive pattern, and improves the gate-to-parameter ratio's effectiveness through      │
│                          │ structural diversity. The alternating design (RX→RZ→CZ→RZ, then RY→RZ→CZ→RZ, then         │
│                          │ RX→RZ→CZ→RZ, then RY→RZ→CZ→RZ) allows the same 2 parameters to explore different rotation │
│                          │ axes in sequence, improving generalization and convergence speed while reducing the depth │
│                          │ penalty of naive repetition.                                                              │
