                         Patch Metadata - Gen 73/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reverse_cz_sweep_before_xx                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses XX gates in a forward-only chain on wires [0,1], [1,2], ...,     │
│                          │ [6,7]. The prior best program (score 0.72) achieved perfect accuracy with only 14         │
│                          │ parameters using CZ gates in the same forward pattern, reaching faster convergence (30    │
│                          │ steps vs 60 steps).                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to prepend a reverse CZ sweep before the XX gates, creating a       │
│                          │ bidirectional entanglement pattern without adding parameters. This approach:              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Doubles entanglement at zero parameter cost**: Add CZ gates on wires [7,6], [6,5],   │
│                          │ ..., [1,0] before the forward XX chain, mirroring the zigzag strategy that worked well in │
│                          │ Gen 62.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Improves parameter efficiency**: The current design uses 20 parameters (ry_shared,   │
│                          │ rz_shared, xx_shared) but struggles with convergence (60 steps). The bidirectional CZ     │
│                          │ pattern can build stronger correlations without additional trainable parameters.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Maintains gate count efficiency**: We're replacing the expensive trainable XX gates  │
│                          │ with fixed CZ gates, reducing the effective parameter count while keeping the total gate  │
│                          │ complexity reasonable.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Addresses the convergence gap**: The prior best (30 steps) vs current (60 steps)     │
│                          │ suggests the current XX parameterization may be harder to optimize. Fixed CZ gates        │
│                          │ provide stable entanglement infrastructure.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The modification prepends fixed reverse CZ sweeps to create a Hadamard-like bidirectional │
│                          │ entanglement before the parametrized XX layer, leveraging the proven strength of the CZ   │
│                          │ chain pattern while keeping parameter economy high.                                       │
