                         Patch Metadata - Gen 76/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sparse_parametric_rings                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses heavily parameter-shared single-qubit rotations combined with   │
│                          │ fixed CZ entanglers, achieving good accuracy but at a moderate gate depth (102). I        │
│                          │ propose a fundamentally different algorithmic strategy: instead of applying the same      │
│                          │ rotation parameters uniformly across all qubits, use **selective parametric two-qubit     │
│                          │ Ising gates (XX, YY, ZZ) on ring patterns** with **minimal single-qubit gates**. This     │
│                          │ reduces parameter sharing overhead while maintaining expressivity through direct          │
│                          │ parametric entanglement.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key differences:                                                                          │
│                          │ 1. **Parametric two-qubit gates** (XX, YY, ZZ) replace some fixed CZ gates, enabling each │
│                          │ interaction pair to have independent learnable angles                                     │
│                          │ 2. **Ring topology** with selective long-range interactions reduces gate count and depth  │
│                          │ while improving connectivity                                                              │
│                          │ 3. **Minimal single-qubit rotation blocks** (alternating RX/RY) provide state preparation │
│                          │ without redundant sharing                                                                 │
│                          │ 4. **Two-block design** keeps depth manageable while achieving the same accuracy          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach should:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Maintain or improve 100% accuracy (current already achieves this)                       │
│                          │ - Significantly reduce gate count and depth through targeted parametric interactions      │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count low while leveraging independent two-qubit parameters for better   │
│                          │ learning dynamics                                                                         │
│                          │ - Improve convergence speed by reducing circuit redundancy                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0185                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
