│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zigzag_two_block_ansatz                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Implement a 2-block ansatz where each block uses an internal zigzag pattern: a            │
│                          │ reverse-direction CZ chain (wires [7,6]→[1,0]) followed by a forward-direction CZ chain   │
│                          │ (wires [0,1]→[6,7]). This doubles the entangling power within each block.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. **Restore 0.72 accuracy**: Zigzag entanglement pattern proven effective in Gen 66      │
│                          │ (alternating blocks) and Gen 62 (varied entanglement)                                     │
│                          │ 2. **Better parameter economy**: Use single shared RZ parameter instead of separate       │
│                          │ rz_pre/rz_post (3 params instead of 20)                                                   │
│                          │ 3. **Faster convergence**: Richer entanglement structure enables learning in fewer steps  │
│                          │ 4. **Maintained expressivity**: Two blocks with internal complexity provides similar      │
│                          │ expressivity to Gen 66's 4 blocks with alternating directions                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The bidirectional CZ sweeps create richer entanglement patterns that improve gradient     │
│                          │ flow and feature extraction on small datasets.                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0243                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
