╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bidirectional_cz_zigzag                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 20 parameters and lower performance (0.68) than prior successful  │
│                          │ designs that used 14 parameters (0.72). The prior successful programs used an alternating │
│                          │ zigzag pattern with bidirectional CZ chains: forward [0→1→2→...→7] then reverse           │
│                          │ [7→6→5→...→0].                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The evidence shows that prepending a reverse-direction CZ sweep before each forward CZ    │
│                          │ chain (as seen in Gen 62-66) drove expressivity gains while maintaining parameter         │
│                          │ efficiency. The current single-block design is missing this bidirectional entanglement,   │
│                          │ which explains the slower convergence (60 vs 30 steps) and higher parameters needed.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit adds a reverse CZ chain immediately before the forward chain, creating the      │
│                          │ proven zigzag pattern. This enables better information flow bidirectionally across the    │
│                          │ qubit line with minimal overhead, improving convergence speed and reducing the need for   │
│                          │ extra parameters.                                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0139                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 8; deleted: 0; modified: 0;                                                        │
